Subject: add a /run tier to the default XKB include path
Source: downstream patch for libxkbcommon 1.7.0
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on adding a compiled-in /run/xkb
  tier between the administrator and vendor entries

xkb_context_include_path_append_default() appends, in order, the two
per-user entries, one "extra" administrator entry
(XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH, else DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH), and one vendor
root entry (XKB_CONFIG_ROOT, else DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_ROOT). FindFileInXkbPath()
then returns the first path in that list that holds the requested file, so
whichever of these directories is searched first for a given basename wins
completely. This manifest passes --prefix=/usr and
-Dxkb-config-root=/usr/share/X11/xkb, so the vendor root is correct, but it
sets neither --sysconfdir nor -Dxkb-config-extra-path, so meson.build
compiles DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH as
get_option('prefix')/get_option('sysconfdir')/'xkb', which resolves to
/usr/etc/xkb: a path under the immutable /usr tree that a machine owner can
never write. There is also no per-boot /run tier at all, so a transient
override (for example one generated by a session or a container) has
nowhere to go.

Passing --sysconfdir=/etc in the manifest fixes the administrator entry: it
makes meson's absolute-path join collapse
get_option('prefix')/get_option('sysconfdir') to exactly /etc, so
DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH becomes /etc/xkb without touching this patch.
Upstream exposes only two path build options (xkb-config-root and
xkb-config-extra-path), so a build option alone cannot add a third,
independently ordered tier; this patch adds one.

meson.build gains a new XKBCONFIGRUNPATH, hardcoded as '/run' / 'xkb'
because /run is a fixed FHS path outside get_option('prefix') and has no
upstream option to override it, and compiles it into config.h as
DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_RUN_PATH alongside the existing root and extra-path
constants. context.h and context.c gain a matching
xkb_context_include_path_get_run_path() accessor, mirroring the existing
get_extra_path()/get_system_path() accessors exactly except that it takes
no environment override: /run is a per-boot overlay the system itself
writes, not a setting an administrator or a caller names directly, and
neither CONFIGURATION.md nor this package's existing XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH
/ XKB_CONFIG_ROOT variables describe one.
xkb_context_include_path_append_default() calls the new accessor between
the existing extra-path and root appends, so the complete default order
becomes: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xkb (or $HOME/.config/xkb), $HOME/.xkb,
XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH or /etc/xkb, /run/xkb, then XKB_CONFIG_ROOT or the
vendor root. xkb_context_include_path_append() already treats a missing
directory as a silently recorded "failed" include rather than an error, so
an absent /run/xkb or /etc/xkb is not a new failure mode; this patch does
not touch that function. XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH and XKB_CONFIG_ROOT keep
their exact upstream meaning: each replaces only its own entry and neither
disables another tier.

diff -urN a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -51,6 +51,11 @@
     XKBCONFIGEXTRAPATH = get_option('prefix')/get_option('sysconfdir')/'xkb'
 endif

+# The XKB runtime overlay. Nex readers merge /etc, /run, and /usr with the
+# administrator tier taking priority; this is the /run tier and has no
+# upstream build option because it sits outside get_option('prefix').
+XKBCONFIGRUNPATH = '/run' / 'xkb'
+
 # The X locale directory for compose.
 XLOCALEDIR = get_option('x-locale-root')
 if XLOCALEDIR == ''
@@ -74,6 +79,7 @@
 system_ext_define = '#define ' + system_extensions
 configh_data.set_quoted('DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_ROOT', XKBCONFIGROOT)
 configh_data.set_quoted('DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_EXTRA_PATH', XKBCONFIGEXTRAPATH)
+configh_data.set_quoted('DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_RUN_PATH', XKBCONFIGRUNPATH)
 configh_data.set_quoted('XLOCALEDIR', XLOCALEDIR)
 configh_data.set_quoted('DEFAULT_XKB_RULES', get_option('default-rules'))
 configh_data.set_quoted('DEFAULT_XKB_MODEL', get_option('default-model'))
@@ -976,6 +982,7 @@
       'datadir': get_option('datadir'),
       'xkb-config-root': XKBCONFIGROOT,
       'xkb-config-extra-path': XKBCONFIGEXTRAPATH,
+      'xkb-config-run-path': XKBCONFIGRUNPATH,
       'xlocaledir': XLOCALEDIR,
     }, section: 'Directories')
     summary({
diff -urN a/src/context.c b/src/context.c
--- a/src/context.c
+++ b/src/context.c
@@ -84,6 +84,13 @@
 }

 const char *
+xkb_context_include_path_get_run_path(struct xkb_context *ctx)
+{
+    (void) ctx;
+    return DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_RUN_PATH;
+}
+
+const char *
 xkb_context_include_path_get_system_path(struct xkb_context *ctx)
 {
     const char *root = xkb_context_getenv(ctx, "XKB_CONFIG_ROOT");
@@ -128,6 +135,11 @@

     extra = xkb_context_include_path_get_extra_path(ctx);
     ret |= xkb_context_include_path_append(ctx, extra);
+    /* /run sits between the administrator and vendor tiers and has no
+     * environment override: it is a per-boot overlay the system itself
+     * writes, not a setting an administrator or a caller names directly. */
+    ret |= xkb_context_include_path_append(ctx,
+                                            xkb_context_include_path_get_run_path(ctx));
     root = xkb_context_include_path_get_system_path(ctx);
     ret |= xkb_context_include_path_append(ctx, root);

diff -urN a/src/context.h b/src/context.h
--- a/src/context.h
+++ b/src/context.h
@@ -71,6 +71,9 @@
 xkb_context_include_path_get_extra_path(struct xkb_context *ctx);

 const char *
+xkb_context_include_path_get_run_path(struct xkb_context *ctx);
+
+const char *
 xkb_context_include_path_get_system_path(struct xkb_context *ctx);

